## Artifact pipeline

When asked to generate software definition artifacts, follow this sequence:

1. Overview + Lean Canvas → docs/product-overview.md  
   (If the user prompt or master prompt specifies another path — e.g.
   `docs/domain-brief.md` — use that path.)
2. Competitive analysis → docs/competitive-analysis.md
3. Use cases + PlantUML diagrams → docs/use-cases.md
4. Data model + Mermaid erDiagram → docs/data-model.md
5. Architecture explanation + Mermaid diagram → docs/architecture.md
6. C4 model (levels 1, 2, 3) → docs/c4-diagram.md
7. ADRs (one per significant decision) → docs/adr/NNN-title.md

## Subagent delegation map

| Artifact                       | Subagent             |
| ------------------------------ | -------------------- |
| PRD, user stories, Lean Canvas | requirements-analyst |
| Competitive analysis           | requirements-analyst |
| Use cases + PlantUML diagrams  | requirements-analyst |
| Data model + ER diagram        | data-architect       |
| Architecture diagram           | system-architect     |
| C4 diagram (all levels)        | system-architect     |
| ADR                            | adr-writer           |

## Execution rules

- Read project context exclusively from the user's prompt.
- Flag ambiguities with [ASSUMPTION: ...] and continue without stopping.
- Never invent requirements not present in the prompt.
- Save every artifact to docs/ unless explicitly told otherwise.
- Confirm each file is written before moving to the next artifact.
